    kind: invariant  # 0a50
    title: "python CFG: an if-statement with two or more alternatives (elif/elif, elif/else) walks only the first; later arms are absent from the CFG, so def/use, DDG edges and the taint walk never see them (3-10% of Python functions forfeit)"  # 0a50
    status: violated  # 0a50
    priority: 2  # 0a50
    parent:  # 0a50
    tags:  # 0a50
    - taint  # 0a50
    - analysis_quality  # 0a50
    - python  # 0a50
    - ddg  # 0a50
    isbefore: []  # 0a50
    duplicate_of: []  # 0a50
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 0a50
    pr_ref:  # 0a50
    description: "**Found 2026-11-04** while measuring the DDG edge count of django's `regex_helper.normalize` (dev 007be3f02e) for the readability panel (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/readability_panel_11042026/`): 106 lines, seven state variables, and `solve_reaching_defs` returned 14 edges over 6 variables; `cfg.uncovered_semantic_lines` listed lines 86-182, the whole if/elif chain after its first `elif` arm.\n\n**Minimal repro** (`readability_panel_11042026/elif_repro.py`, probe `probe_ddg.py` there; both run with the installed checkout):\n\n```\ndef plain_chain(ch, out):\n    if ch == \"a\":\n        out.append(\"A\")\n    elif ch == \"b\":\n        out.append(\"B\")\n    elif ch == \"c\":      # line 6: not in the CFG\n        out.append(\"C\")  # line 7: not in the CFG\n    else:\n        out.append(\"Z\")  # line 9: not in the CFG\n    return out\n```\n\n`uncovered_semantic_lines` = {6, 7, 9}. The same for a chain whose second arm raises, and for a chain inside `while True` inside `try` (arms 3, 4 and the else lost). The FIRST `elif` is walked, but as straight-line code: its condition and body are recorded as sequential statements on the `false` edge of the `if`, with no branch between them.\n\n**Root cause.** tree-sitter-python puts every `elif_clause` and the `else_clause` under the `if_statement`'s REPEATED `alternative` field. `cfg_nodes/python.yaml` maps `conditional: if_statement` with `false_child: \"field:alternative\"`, and `CfgBuilder._process_conditional` (cfg.py ~1360) reads it through `_find_child`, which returns the first alternative only; the mapping has no `elif_clause` conditional, so even that one alternative is handed to `_process_node` and decomposed as sequential statements. Every other DDG language (c, go, java, rust, typescript) nests `else if` as an `if_statement` inside a single `alternative`, so the one-child read is correct there and this is Python-only among the shipped mappings.\n\n**Blast radius** (`elif_census.py`, `elif_census.txt`; a function counts when an `if_statement` in its body has two or more `alternative` children):\n\n| tree | functions | with a 2+-alternative chain | chains | arms never walked |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| packages/hypergumbo-core/src | 3093 | 104 (3.4%) | 118 | 213 |\n| packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src | 1556 | 159 (10.2%) | 207 | 420 |\n| django/django | 9484 | 326 (3.4%) | 353 | 581 |\n| httpx/httpx | 446 | 21 (4.7%) | 22 | 39 |\n\n**Consequences.** (1) Every such function has uncovered call nodes, so it lands in `RepoDdg.forfeit_refutation` (WI-joluk): the taint walk may never return False over it, and every same-function sink reads approximate under ADR-0017 mixed mode. That is disclosed, not hidden, but it is 3-10% of Python functions forfeited for a builder gap. (2) Definitions and uses in the lost arms produce no DDG edges, so a flow through an `elif` arm beyond the first is invisible to the walk (a seed used only there reads `source_not_tracked`). (3) The first `elif`'s body is unconditional on the false path, so a definition there kills an earlier one without a branch, which can hide a reaching definition from a later use.\n\n**Fix shape (structural).** In `_process_conditional`, read `_find_children(node, mapping.false_child)` and chain the alternatives: an alternative whose type has its own `ConditionalMapping` (add `elif_clause` to python.yaml with `condition_child: field:condition`, `true_child: field:consequence`, no `false_child`) becomes a condition block with a `true` edge to its consequence and a `false` edge to the NEXT alternative; the last alternative (an `else_clause`, or any type without a mapping) is processed as today. For the five nesting grammars `_find_children` returns one child and nothing changes; pin that with a test per language. Sibling sweep NOT done yet: Python `try_statement` (repeated `except_clause`) and `match_statement` (repeated `case_clause`) are also repeated-child shapes; check they are read with `_find_children` before closing.\n\n**Pre-registered verification.** After the fix: `plain_chain` and the two variants have no uncovered lines and the expected true/false edges; `normalize` gains edges over `result`, `ch`, `escaped`, `non_capturing_groups`, `num_args`, `consume_next`, `terminal_char`, `name`, `count`, `start`, `inner` (expected well above 14); the self-tree `forfeit_refutation` set shrinks by about the 104 core + 159 mainstream functions that have no OTHER uncovered construct (measure before/after with `build_repo_ddg` over packages/*/src); the self-claims gate (`scripts/check-self-claims`) stays at 23 `confirmed_with_caveats` with the same or fewer approximate sinks. Corpus delta on the io-manifest / bakeoff repos: not measured, to be measured as an A/B on the DDG edge-producing function count (never the total)."  # 0a50
    fields:  # 0a50
      statement: "Every arm of a Python if/elif/else chain is a CFG branch: each elif_clause is a condition block with a true edge to its consequence and a false edge to the next alternative, and the else_clause is the last false branch."  # 0a50
      root_cause: "tree-sitter-python puts every elif_clause and the else_clause under the if_statement's REPEATED alternative field; CfgBuilder._process_conditional reads mapping.false_child through _find_child, which returns the first alternative only, and cfg_nodes/python.yaml maps no elif_clause conditional, so the one alternative that is walked is decomposed as sequential statements."  # 0a50
